# Independent display and cutover result

Reviewed adopted HEAD 2f3545ecad601bc19e19c0d3495ee6fd11eedb36. No blocking finding in the chapter 17 migration scope.

- Actual old GitHub blob: all eight aliases match unique real IDs and their original headings. Actual adopted GitHub blob: all eight legacy and seven semantic anchors are unique, and settled navigation reaches the corresponding positions. Adjacent legacy/semantic names reach the same position; the final heading stops at the document bottom. The first short-wait measurement is retained separately.
- Original, adopted Markdown, and live GitHub preserve the same 21 code spans exactly. Two tables preserve 3 and 8 data rows and their column associations. All five external KaTeX references and chapter 18 relative reference are retained. The live chapter 18 href points to the same adopted commit.
- Generated HTML tested in Chromium, Firefox, and WebKit with JavaScript disabled at 375 and 1280 pixels under a nonroot URL: HTTP 200, no failed requests, no horizontal document overflow, 703 Ruby instances, supplied CSS applied, 21 exact code spans, both tables preserved, and chapter 18 navigation works. Representative screenshots were visually inspected for narrow heading/prose, narrow failure table, and wide page. The seven stable HTML Section IDs are unique and navigation reaches each section.
- Direct file viewing succeeds in Chromium and Firefox with offline=True. Direct file viewing also succeeds in WebKit with its normal context and both HTTP and HTTPS requests blocked; no HTTP(S) requests occurred, local CSS applied, stable navigation and chapter 18 movement worked. WebKit offline=True produced a runner internal error and is not marked passed; synthetic local-byte fulfillment was an additional separate check, not the basis of the final direct-file result.
- HTML first/second outputs are byte-identical for all 13 files. The successful receipt starts with zero usage and selects allocation 1,000,000,000, Work 400,000,000, Nodes 20,000,000. Observed usage is allocation 762,304,126, Work 362,735,172, Nodes 13,880,291. This supports the explicit finite allocation-only adjustment; the earlier 750M stop remains a failed operation.

This reviews the migrated specification page and its artifacts, not implementation of the KaTeX runtime acceptance groups described by that page. Human screen-reader operation was not performed. HTML exposes stable semantic Section IDs; Markdown legacy aliases were checked on actual GitHub, not claimed as HTML IDs. The existing generic HTML title and unset document lang are unchanged renderer behavior, so this is not a claim of universal accessibility compliance.

Evidence resides entirely under .tmp/review17-display. No tracked source was edited by this reviewer. seal.json records evidence file hashes; every individual file is below 1 MB.
